        "kind": "source_conditions",
        "clauses": [
          {
            "text": "Use this capability to review staged changes, working-tree diffs, or git commits before commit, push, merge, or release. It is a review gate: it reads the actual diff, finds correctness and scope risks, checks commit-message quality, flags over-engineering, and gives a clear readiness decision.",
            "heading": "Purpose",
            "source": {
              "path": "ssot/engos-quality-code-review.md",
              "start_line": 11,
              "end_line": 11,
              "sha256": "8ea2082a3278c50c8e7ff92b7c14b2f404fa882ca362b2452cfd7e80a0c8bc85"
            }
          },
          {
            "text": "Use this before you create a commit, before you push a branch, before an MR/PR is merged, or after a fix commit has been prepared. Do not use this capability to modify files or apply reviewer feedback; use `engos-delivery-address-code-review` when the user wants selected PR/MR review comments implemented.",
            "heading": "Purpose",
            "source": {
              "path": "ssot/engos-quality-code-review.md",
              "start_line": 13,
              "end_line": 13,
              "sha256": "8ea2082a3278c50c8e7ff92b7c14b2f404fa882ca362b2452cfd7e80a0c8bc85"
            }
          },
          {
            "text": "1. Read the complete `review` route in `resources/resource-map.json`: `resources/references/review-targets.md` and its findings schema. Use the existing bundled `resources/scripts/load_module.py --route review` when available, or read both files directly. Missing or unread required resources make the review incomplete.\n2. Capture the exact staged diff, working-tree diff, commit, or branch diff under review; bind it and relevant source/consumer reads to the target as specified in that reference.\n3. Read the commit message and the actual diff before making any judgment.\n4. Check message quality, scope alignment, and implementation complexity.\n5. Record findings with stable IDs, severity, precise location, changed-cause evidence, verified consumer evidence for introduced breakage, impact, repair, and disposition.\n6. End with ready, blocked, or split required for a complete review; use unverifiable when evidence or review coverage is incomplete. Review judgment grants no repair, publication, merge, or release authority.",
            "heading": "Workflow",
            "source": {
              "path": "ssot/engos-quality-code-review.md",
              "start_line": 66,
              "end_line": 71,
              "sha256": "8ea2082a3278c50c8e7ff92b7c14b2f404fa882ca362b2452cfd7e80a0c8bc85"
            }
          },
          {
            "text": "Use this capability when the user asks for any of the following, even without naming the skill:\n- review the latest commit\n- review my staged changes before I commit\n- review this diff before I push\n- check whether this diff is too broad\n- judge whether AI-generated changes are over-engineered\n- tell me if this commit message and change scope are strong enough to merge",
            "heading": "Invocation Hints",
            "source": {
              "path": "ssot/engos-quality-code-review.md",
              "start_line": 97,
              "end_line": 103,
              "sha256": "8ea2082a3278c50c8e7ff92b7c14b2f404fa882ca362b2452cfd7e80a0c8bc85"
            }
          }
        ]
      },
